# Witness: a review document that pins a source file to a line number

Everything else about this fragment is well formed. The one fault is the row below, which cites a
range rather than a member - the form this repository has already watched rot. The annotations
shifted every line in every file, and the citation the worksheet carried went stale unnoticed,
because a rule that checks identifiers and counts never asks whether a cited line means anything.

The scan is the whole document and no longer one kind of row. Restricting it to the worksheet's
`Read` rows was safe only while the worksheet was the only document that pointed anywhere; a
pointer in an evidence bundle or in the status ledger rots in exactly the same way, and was read
by nothing.

## Where to look

| Area | Read |
|---|---|
| Bounded reading | `src/Broiler.VM.Binary/VmBoundedAllocator.cs` 34-68, and the governing record |
| Allocation guard | `src/Broiler.VM.Binary/VmBoundedReader.cs:57` |
